Z||000000||p4n1c||05-03-2001||09:45 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/olrusty2.jpg">  <P>This is my new car which is a hand me down from my parents.  They've had it since new in March of 1989, it was one of the last of the '88 model year.  It's an '88 Cutlass Supreme International with the Chevy 2.8l V6 DIS 130hp engine.  It has over 400,000kms(250,000 miles) on her and she is still running strong except for sloppy shift between park and reverse.  As you can see though she needs some body work and new wheels.  All in all it will cost me less then $1000(Canadian) to get her back into shape mechanically.<P>I decided this instead of a Fiero because:<P>a) it's free, which allows me to use the money I was going to buy a car with, to bring it back to it's original form then modify it<BR>b) the insurance and registration will be kept under my dad(I will be principle driver) which means less $$$ for me to have to spend out each month<BR>c) the car is still licensed so no safety or e-cert has to be done<P>I do still plan on buying a Fiero later on when I have more money and a house so that I can actually work on it.  My apartment building doesn't allow people to work on their cars in the underground garage.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just thought I'd share that and I'll still be lurking around here, because this forum is fun.<P>Here's another pic of what I want it to look like(Picture is photo edited by Shawn Lin of the W-Body page( <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/gm_w_body" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/gm_w_body</A> )).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/olds-head.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||05-04-2001||10:04 AM||||Cool car!<BR>I've driven one of those. (Not too sure if it was an International, or not.) Had tons of power and was a lot of fun to drive.<BR>Best of luck!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||14
Z||000002||Formula||05-04-2001||10:42 AM||||I was looking into buying one of those around 2 years ago.  For some reason I thought it had a 3.8 but maybe that was a newer version...<P>those cars can look sweet if you keep it clean (no decals) and monotone!<P>btw.... cant wait to see modded pics<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||p4n1c||05-04-2001||10:43 AM||||Thanks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>She's a little beat up right now, but I'm going to fix her up good.<P>First planned mods are:<BR>-Fix the air intake, it is a little piece of rectangular plastic behind the headlight right now, I want to add a cold air intake or at least make it less restrictive<P>-Less restrictive cat and muffler<P>-8.8mm wires and new plugs<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||7
Z||000004||p4n1c||05-04-2001||10:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>For some reason I thought it had a 3.8 but maybe that was a newer version...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The '91 or '92 International was the first one with the 3.4 DOHC.  210hp and monotone.  All the other Internationals from 88 -&gt; 90 had either a 2.8 or 3.1.<P>I would like the 3.4 in mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The car weighs around 3200lbs.  Which isn't bad compared to the original Cutlass which was around 4000+.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
